= State continuity (simple) =

'''State continuity''' means that we can explain how a system got from an earlier condition to its current condition.

For a computer program, this may mean restoring the correct saved data after a restart. For an AI agent, it may also mean ensuring the data belongs to the right agent. In biology, cells change their material while keeping parts of their organization; offspring inherit genetic information without being the same organism as a parent.

Two copies can have identical information but still be two different systems. That is why '''copying data is not the same as preserving identity'''.

